  "response": "### Executive Synthesis\n\nThis pre-performance adversarial review examines the methodological design, evidence artifacts, and freeze harness for **Q089** (`T-2026-09-28-089-*`), intended as a clean, fresh, symbol-disjoint validation of the frozen Q069 candidate bank (`C7`–`C11`).\n\nWhile Q089 enforces strict evidence sequencing (Coverage $\\to$ Input Freeze $\\to$ PIT $\\to$ Performance), several subtle methodological failure modes could compromise scientific validity prior to performance execution:\n\n1. **Retroactive Corporate Action Lookahead in `adjusted_close.csv`:** Adjusted close series computed via global back-adjustment embed future dividend payments and split ratios into historical prices before decision dates.\n2. **Network Decoupling Boundary in `q089_input_freeze.py`:** Generating `adjusted_close.csv` via live network fetching (`fetch_adjusted_close`) rather than purely transforming the byte-frozen snapshot creates a cross-runner reproducibility vulnerability.\n3. **Geometry/Truncation Ambiguity:** The coverage result recorded 3,704 common trading sessions, whereas the input bundle enforces exactly 3,500 rows without an explicit immutable slicing rule recorded in the manifest.\n4. **Symbol Disjointness & Quarantine Leakage:** Prior quarantined runs (Q085, Q086) must not contaminate the discovery pool, and symbol exclusion must be deterministically verifiable against the global registry.\n\n---\n\n### Primary Methodological Failure Modes\n\n#### 1. Point-in-Time Contamination via Global Adjusted Close\n* **Failure Mechanism:** The candidate bank (`C7_LOW_MAX_21`, `C8_LOW_IDIO_VOL_273`, `C9_LONG_TERM_REVERSAL_756`, `C10_TREND_EFFICIENCY_63`, `C11_VOLUME_CONFIRMED_TREND_126`) relies on historical price ratios, idiosyncratic volatilities, and returns. If calculated from standard full-sample adjusted close data, prices at $t < T$ are adjusted by dividend distributions occurring between $t$ and the end of the study window (2025-09-24).\n* **I